255
00:10:49,839 --> 00:10:52,640
assume an ephemeral secure session so

256
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:54,880
they don't have to save the nonces but if

257
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:58,160
you want something like multisig

258
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:01,279
that can span multiple sessions then

259
00:11:01,279 --> 00:11:02,880
your host because now you have to store

260
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:06,079
all those nonces forever get replayed.

261
00:11:06,079 --> 00:11:08,240
When you look at Replay

262
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:11,120
Attack Protection, when you go away from

263
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:14,480
ephemeral interactions to things that

264
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:16,480
have to last for long periods of time,

265
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:18,320
most of the existing mechanisms just

266
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,600
don't work. They just

267
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:22,000
don't scale. You have to remember things

268
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,399
forever or you have to start to build

269
00:11:24,399 --> 00:11:26,000
provable caches.

270
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,040
– Statistically random with large

271
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:32,870
– Yeah.

